{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 4, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a powerful figure in the 12th century known for his military prowess and political acumen. He ruled as Count of Tripoli from 1101 to 1146 effectively consolidating power and expanding the territory under his control. His reign marked a period of significant growth and prosperity for the County of Tripoli making it a major power in the Levant.\n\n*Early Life and Ascension* Raymond was the son of Raymond I Count of Tripoli. He inherited the County upon his father's death in 1101. Immediately upon assuming the throne Raymond faced challenges from both internal dissent and external threats. He skillfully navigated these complexities establishing a stable government and fostering alliances. He was known for his military leadership and his ability to raise and command effective armies. His early years were marked by consolidating his authority and dealing with rebellious factions within the County.\n\nRaymond III’s reign witnessed a flourishing of Tripoli's economy and culture. He actively promoted trade and agriculture transforming the County into a major center of commerce. Tripoli became a vital port facilitating trade between Europe the Middle East and North Africa. This economic prosperity allowed Raymond to invest in infrastructure and support the arts and sciences. He also oversaw the construction of several important buildings including the Great Mosque of Tripoli a testament to his patronage of Islamic architecture.\n\n*Military Campaigns and Conflicts* Raymond III was a renowned military leader who engaged in numerous campaigns to protect Tripoli's interests and expand its territory. He successfully defended the County against attacks from various enemies including the Normans the Seljuk Turks and the Fatimids. His military victories solidified Tripoli’s position as a significant power in the region. He also participated in the Crusades although his involvement was often less direct compared to other Crusader states. Raymond's military campaigns were characterized by his strategic thinking and his ability to adapt to changing circumstances. He employed a combination of diplomacy and military force to achieve his objectives.\n\nRaymond III's reign ended in 1146 when he died after a long and eventful life. He left behind a prosperous and powerful County of Tripoli. His legacy as a skilled ruler a capable military commander and a patron of the arts and sciences continues to be celebrated. His impact on the history of the Levant is undeniable. He is remembered as one of the most important rulers of the County of Tripoli. His efforts contributed significantly to the County's growth and stability during a turbulent period in history.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.1434636116027832}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -6.854299135738984e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.50339189733495e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.0874934121966362}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.029306435957551003}, {"token": "▁powerful", "logprob": -0.5966804027557373}, {"token": "▁figure", "logprob": -1.6292102336883545}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": -0.02329634316265583}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.0035798768512904644}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.6596265435218811}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -0.0014444880653172731}, {"token": "th", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁century", "logprob": -0.031712405383586884}, {"token": "▁known", "logprob": -1.3300848007202148}, {"token": "▁for", "logprob": -0.011888484470546246}, {"token": "▁his", "logprob": -0.0047684283927083015}, {"token": "▁military", "logprob": -0.057362452149391174}, {"token": "▁prowess", "logprob": -0.11130551248788834}, {"token": "▁and", "logprob": -0.06441149860620499}, {"token": "▁politi